Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:06.51,Default,,0,0,0,,RL Triage Agent investigates robot learning failures. It\Nconnects model hypotheses to inspections,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.51,0:00:09.01,Default,,0,0,0,,registered repairs, and behavioral tests.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.00,0:00:16.70,Default,,0,0,0,,First, a freshly captured normal policy in Isaac Lab. This\Nis a simulated Go two robot, following a
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.70,0:00:19.68,Default,,0,0,0,,motion command on Nebius L forty S compute.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.50,0:00:28.42,Default,,0,0,0,,With the known F one reward defect, the robot barely follows\Nthat command. These are normal and
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.42,0:00:31.55,Default,,0,0,0,,faulty captures, not a before and after repair video.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.00,0:00:41.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Now the application replays a separate, completed P P O\Nepoch failure. The public source files are
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.05,0:00:46.39,Default,,0,0,0,,hash verified. Both policies survive twenty seconds, but\Nlinear tracking error rises from zero point
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.39,0:00:50.67,Default,,0,0,0,,one four six to one point one six nine meters per second.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.00,0:00:59.03,Default,,0,0,0,,The recorded Nemotron response first selects the reward\Ninspection. It returns normal. The following
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.03,0:01:05.07,Default,,0,0,0,,inspections use the registered sequence, rather than more\Nmodel choices. This matters: a plausible
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.07,0:01:08.09,Default,,0,0,0,,first hypothesis is not a confirmed mechanism.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.00,0:01:16.90,Default,,0,0,0,,A short optimizer inspection finds the discrepancy. Five\Nepochs and four minibatches should produce
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.90,0:01:22.80,Default,,0,0,0,,twenty optimizer steps per update. The faulty configuration\Nproduces only four. These are fresh
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.80,0:01:27.02,Default,,0,0,0,,three update inspections, not measurements loaded from the\Ntrained checkpoint.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.00,0:01:34.35,Default,,0,0,0,,The registered correction restores the configured epoch\Ncount. The recorded approval chain is
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.35,0:01:39.69,Default,,0,0,0,,proposed, approved, consumed, then receipt. Training\Nrestarts with a different seed. This replay
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.69,0:01:45.04,Default,,0,0,0,,reads those artifacts; it does not issue a new approval or\Nrun training.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.00,0:01:51.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Recovery is tested separately across twenty six fixed\Nconditions. The corrected policy's linear
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.95,0:01:58.05,Default,,0,0,0,,tracking error is zero point one four eight meters per\Nsecond, near the normal control. Its
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.05,0:02:01.48,Default,,0,0,0,,checkpoint hash and evaluation metrics match the recorded\Nsummary.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.00,0:02:11.35,Default,,0,0,0,,A separate compound defect needs another loop. In two\Ndevelopment seeds, the first correction is
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.35,0:02:17.27,Default,,0,0,0,,insufficient. Both pass after the second correction, in\Nopposite orders. These are known defect
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.27,0:02:21.93,Default,,0,0,0,,development results, not evidence of unseen fault\Ngeneralization or model superiority.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.00,0:02:29.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Simulation uses Brev provisioned Nebius L forty S compute.\NNemotron inference uses NVIDIA's hosted
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.24,0:02:35.48,Default,,0,0,0,,endpoint. Token Factory calls are not yet demonstrated.\NIssued promotional credits are not a
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.48,0:02:36.81,Default,,0,0,0,,verified redeemed balance.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.00,0:02:45.21,Default,,0,0,0,,The open source package includes an English replay, source\Nhashes, and a C P U verifier. Inspect the
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.21,0:02:48.42,Default,,0,0,0,,evidence, test the mechanism, and evaluate the repair.
